---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const effective = 'August 22, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern use of the Forger Digital Solutions website."
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Terms of Use</span>
  </nav>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="doc__updated">Last updated: {effective}</p>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="doc__lead">
      These terms govern your use of the Forger Digital Solutions ("FDS") website at
      {' '}{siteConfig.siteUrl}. By using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please
      don't use the site.
    </p>

    <div class="doc__body">
      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is an informational showcase for FDS and its projects. Content is provided for
        general information only and may change or be removed at any time without notice. Project
        descriptions reflect work in progress and are not commitments, guarantees, or offers.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The FDS name, logo, branding, site design, and written content are the property of Forger
        Digital Solutions unless otherwise noted, and are protected by applicable law. You may view
        and share links to the site, but you may not copy, reuse, or redistribute our branding or
        content as your own without permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party names, trademarks, engines, and platforms referenced on the site belong to
        their respective owners. Their appearance indicates use or experimentation, not
        endorsement, sponsorship, certification, or partnership.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>use the site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of these terms;</li>
        <li>attempt to disrupt, attack, or gain unauthorized access to the site or its hosting;</li>
        <li>misrepresent your affiliation with FDS.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to third-party services such as GitHub, YouTube, Discord, Ko-fi, and Cash
        App. We don't control those services and aren't responsible for their content, policies,
        or availability. Your use of them is governed by their terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Support contributions</h2>
      <p>
        Voluntary support for FDS development and hardware is handled through Ko-fi and Cash App
        and is subject to each service's own terms. Contributions help sustain independent
        development and operations and are not a purchase of any product, service, or deliverable
        unless expressly stated. They are generally non-refundable except where required by law.
        Contributions should not be assumed to be tax-deductible charitable donations. Hardware
        donations are coordinated privately by email and are not guaranteed to be accepted.
        Community-project funding, described on the Community Impact page, is not active and is
        kept separate from development and hardware support.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, whether
        express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do
        not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, FDS will not be liable for any indirect,
        incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the
        site.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New Jersey, United States, without
        regard to its conflict-of-laws rules.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the site after changes take
        effect means you accept the revised terms. We'll revise the "last updated" date above when
        we make changes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="doc__back" href="/">&larr; Back home</a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc__back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 3rem; font: 700 .76rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
</style>
